Introduction to Geochronology — Pieter Vermeesch (@geo-geochron: 0, is #reference, #part-of @geo-sources) { r_30AEAXYK3VV89FDX1TF9ZKJ84J
Pieter Vermeesch. Introduction to Geochronology, lecture notes for the University College London isotope-geology module. [Author's contents and complete sections](https://pieter-vermeesch.es.ucl.ac.uk/geotopes/indexli1.html) · [Author's source/revision repository](https://github.com/pvermees/geotopes).

Read the entire notes and exercises during the advanced time study: radioactivity, analytical techniques, parent/daughter systems, isochrons, U-Pb/concordia, K-Ar, thermochronology, cosmogenic/U-series methods, error propagation, and programming practicals. This is a later substantial academic treatment, with mathematical preparation followed where actually used.

The author's published sections and repository are freely readable. Preserve the actual version and any stated content/code rights; a public repository alone is not an assertion of unrestricted reuse. The older author-host root failed, while the current explicit contents and source locations worked. Author, institutional/course identity, structure, and access checked on 29 October 2026. No lecture collection or software is copied here.

